From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: audio-graph-card2: fix double put of multi port nodes

graph_link_init() takes a reference on each port with ep_to_port().
For a multi link, graph_get_next_multi_ep() drops the reference on the
port it is handed before moving to the next one, so the following
of_node_put() releases the node a second time:

  OF: ERROR: of_node_release() detected bad of_node_put() on /sound-speakers/multi/ports@1/port@0

Drop the extra puts.

Fixes: e935f903ab9b ("ASoC: audio-graph-card2: use correct endpoint when getting link parameters")
---
 sound/soc/generic/audio-graph-card2.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/generic/audio-graph-card2.c b/sound/soc/generic/audio-graph-card2.c
--- a/sound/soc/generic/audio-graph-card2.c
+++ b/sound/soc/generic/audio-graph-card2.c
@@ -754,7 +754,6 @@
 	if (graph_lnk_is_multi(port_cpu)) {
 		multi_cpu_port = port_cpu;
 		ep_cpu = graph_get_next_multi_ep(&multi_cpu_port, multi_cpu_port_idx++);
-		of_node_put(port_cpu);
 		port_cpu = ep_to_port(ep_cpu);
 	} else {
 		of_node_get(ep_cpu);
@@ -764,7 +763,6 @@
 	if (graph_lnk_is_multi(port_codec)) {
 		multi_codec_port = port_codec;
 		ep_codec = graph_get_next_multi_ep(&multi_codec_port, multi_codec_port_idx++);
-		of_node_put(port_codec);
 		port_codec = ep_to_port(ep_codec);
 	} else {
 		of_node_get(ep_codec);
